<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Jalen Suggs Paid $32.4m on His Rookie Extension?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Suggs is paid <strong>$32.4m</strong> because Orlando extended him off his rookie contract at a flat number, and wrote the money to fall each year.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went fifth in 2021 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$29.96m</strong>.</li>
<li>The club exercised both options on it, in 2022 and 2023.</li>
<li>The extension is <strong>$150.5m</strong> over five years, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>It started at <strong>$35m</strong> and comes down from there.</li>
<li>He is one of four Orlando players earning more than <strong>$30m</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has never been paid by another club.</p>

